      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-320865",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-x+4 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+2x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-{x}^{2}-2x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4x+8}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we conclude the following:\n\n| $3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} | $-\\,\\,$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+2$ |  | $x+2$ |  |  |  |"
